{#
  The playground hub — the de-versioned home page (the plan's own
  disposition for /v6/unified-guidance: "keep as-is, becomes / (home)";
  here that's /playground/hub, since the site's actual "/" still serves
  the frozen versions index — see the playground build's own decisions
  log for why). Carried over unchanged from /v6/unified-guidance, which had
  already done the real consolidation work this page needed (merging the
  old /v6/find-guidance and /v6/all-guidance-docs pair into one screen with
  four tabs) — only hrefs are re-pointed at /playground/... routes below.
  One content panel per tab (data-tab-panel), only one visible at a time.

  The tabs themselves are real govuk-tabs markup (.govuk-tabs/
  __list/__list-item/__list-item--selected/__tab/__panel/__panel--hidden —
  see node_modules/govuk-frontend/dist/govuk/components/tabs/), hand-
  written rather than rendered through the govukTabs() macro or
  initialised via its data-module="govuk-tabs" JS: this page needs two
  behaviours the packaged component doesn't support — a second, unrelated
  element (the search-bar row above the tabs) toggling in step with the
  active tab, and ?tab=-query-param deep-linking rather than tabs.js' own
  #hash-based one — so pageScripts below drives the exact same visual
  states (the --selected/--hidden classes) with its own click handler
  instead, same generic data-tab-button/data-tab-panel wiring every other
  hand-rolled tab set in this project already uses (originally established
  on editor-2-3-view.html). role="tablist"/"tab"/"tabpanel"/aria-selected/
  aria-controls/aria-labelledby are set directly in this markup rather
  than left for tabs.js to add at runtime, since that script never runs
  here. Deliberately no .govuk-tabs__title ("Contents", the component's
  own no-JS/small-screen anchor-link fallback heading) — each panel
  already opens with its own heading (see below), and every tab in this
  project needs JS to work at all (activeTab is still correctly resolved
  server-side with no JS, but switching tabs after that requires the click
  handler below) — a second "Contents" heading here would be redundant,
  not a genuine accessibility gap: govuk-tabs__panel--hidden's own
  display:none is itself gated behind .govuk-frontend-supported (added to
  <body> by the kit's own boilerplate script only once JS actually runs),
  so on the rare visit with JS unavailable every panel still falls back to
  showing in full, stacked, exactly as intended by the real component.

  Every row on every tab is exactly the same session-backed data the two
  old pages already built, read the exact same way — nothing here
  recomputes or reshapes it further:
    - recentlyOpenedDocuments/savedGuidanceDocuments: view-model.js calls
      guidanceLists.buildFindGuidanceRows(guidanceLists.getRecentlyOpened/
      getSavedGuidance(req)) — app/data/guidance-lists.js, shared,
      unmodified, with v2/v5's own /find-guidance routes.
    - editingDocuments/awaitingApprovalDocuments: view-model.js calls
      buildManageGuidanceRows(req) — app/data/manage-guidance.js, shared,
      unmodified, with v5's own manage-guidance routes.
  The two are session-independent — neither reads the other's
  req.session.data keys — so merging them into one screen is a pure UI
  change, not a data migration.

  activeTab (view-model.js, resolved from ?tab=, one of
  recently-opened/saved-guidance/editing/awaiting-approval, defaulting to
  recently-opened for anything else) decides which button/panel render
  already active server-side, so there is no flash of the wrong tab before
  pageScripts' own click handler attaches. The two "Remove" flows that used
  to return to /v6/find-guidance#<anchor> or /v6/all-guidance-docs#editing
  now redirect straight to /v6/unified-guidance?tab=<the tab they were on>
  instead (see those two controllers' own postRemove) — everywhere else
  that still links to the old URLs (breadcrumbs elsewhere in the app,
  mostly) is left pointing at them deliberately: one extra redirect hop,
  landing on the default tab, an accepted trade-off rather than a
  file-by-file fix-up.

  documentsTable/manageGuidanceTable and versionTags below are copied
  verbatim from find-guidance.html/all-guidance-docs.html (now
  app/views/v6/find-guidance/ and app/views/v6/all-guidance-docs/'s own
  retired templates) — same markup, same hrefs (including
  ?from=find-guidance on the Recently opened/Saved guidance title links,
  which document-overview.html's own breadcrumb logic still checks for
  specifically — untouched, so left exactly as it was), same column
  asymmetry between Editing (Document name/Version/Last modified/Remove)
  and Awaiting approval (Document name/Version/Publishing checks/Changes
  requested, no Action column) — that split is genuine, not incidental,
  see manageGuidanceTable's own comment below.

  Search bar + always-visible action button sitting above a tabs block
  doesn't fit common/layouts/content.njk's single two-thirds column or
  hub.njk's hero+tiles — extends common/layouts/base.njk directly and
  hand-rolls its own grid, same reasoning app/views/v5/find-guidance/
  page.njk already documents for itself for a similar mismatch.

  No govukBreadcrumbs — this is the site's own front door, nothing above
  it to trail back to, the same "no breadcrumb, this is a landing page"
  choice both retired pages already made for themselves.

  Design refinement pass (the two retired pages' own "Find guidance"/
  "Manage guidance" <h2> headings removed entirely, search bar promoted to
  its own full-width row above the tabs): the old per-tab
  findGuidanceIntro/manageGuidanceIntro blocks (heading + intro text +
  search form, one rendered inside each of the four panels) are now
  findGuidanceSearch/manageGuidanceSearch (intro text + search form only,
  no heading), rendered once each ABOVE .govuk-tabs rather than inside a
  panel — one per tab *group* (Recently opened/Saved guidance share the
  find-guidance search; Editing/Awaiting approval share the
  manage-guidance one), toggled by data-search-group in pageScripts'
  TAB_SEARCH_GROUP map, resolved server-side from activeTab the same way
  panel visibility already is, so there's no flash of the wrong search bar
  either.

  "Create or upload guidance" (previously only shown alongside
  manageGuidanceSearch, i.e. only on the Editing/Awaiting approval tabs)
  moved out to its own always-visible row below the search bar and above
  .govuk-tabs — a global action, not specific to either search
  destination, so it no longer toggles with the tab group. Its own href
  now points at /v6/create-guidance (app/views/v6/create-guidance/) —
  v6's own port of v2's "what would you like to do?" + upload flow — not
  the old, unprefixed /create-guidance (v2's own route) this button
  originally carried over verbatim before that page existed.

  Sidebar+content → horizontal govuk-tabs pass: the four tabs moved from
  a left sidebar of vertical buttons (a hand-rolled, bespoke-styled
  component — first as a Defra-green left-accent list, later a GDS-
  adjacent "translation" of govuk-tabs into a vertical shape) to real
  horizontal govuk-tabs markup sitting directly above the content panel,
  per an explicit request for pixel-exact GDS tab styling rather than a
  vertical reinterpretation of it — see the govuk-tabs paragraph near the
  top of this comment for the markup/behaviour split. The old
  .app-unified-guidance/__sidebar/__nav/__nav-button/__content classes and
  their sidebar/content flex layout are gone entirely, fully superseded by
  .govuk-tabs' own real component CSS (already compiled into
  application.css — GOV.UK Frontend ships every component by default — so
  no new CSS was needed for the tab bar or panel border themselves).
  app/assets/sass/components/_app-unified-guidance.scss (still imported
  under that name in application.scss) now holds only the
  .app-unified-guidance__search search-bar-row rules below.

  Each panel now opens with its own <h2 class="govuk-heading-m"> matching
  its tab's own label exactly ("Recently opened", "Saved guidance",
  "Editing", "Awaiting approval" — no count suffix, unlike the tab label
  text). <h2>, not <h1>: the green banner above already carries the
  page's one real <h1> ("RPA Guidance hub"), so a second <h1> here would be
  a heading-hierarchy/accessibility regression. govuk-heading-m, not -l:
  -l compiles to the same 36px as .defra-home-header__title's own
  font-size at desktop widths (2.25rem, see _typography.scss) — same size
  as the page's actual <h1>, not "noticeably smaller" as intended, despite
  being a visually smaller step on GDS's own scale; -m (24px desktop/18px
  mobile) is unambiguously smaller at every width, while still landing on
  a real GDS heading step rather than a bespoke font-size. (This is also
  why the old per-group "Find guidance"/"Manage guidance" headings this
  replaced, and this page's own first pass at this heading, both used -l —
  neither sat directly under a 36px <h1> the way this one now does.)
  Swaps with the rest of the panel automatically — no separate toggle
  needed, since it lives inside the same govuk-tabs__panel div that
  pageScripts shows/hides via govuk-tabs__panel--hidden.
#}
{% extends "common/layouts/base.njk" %}

{% from "govuk/components/button/macro.njk" import govukButton %}
{% from "govuk/components/input/macro.njk" import govukInput %}
{% from "govuk/components/table/macro.njk" import govukTable %}
{% from "govuk/components/tag/macro.njk" import govukTag %}

{% set pageName = "Guidance hub" %}

{#
  The green "home header" hero — title, description, and an optional
  navigation tabs list. This is a page-local copy of the markup
  partials/defra-header.njk already renders for /v6/unified-guidance under
  its own isV6Home flag (set in app/views/legacy/routes.js), not a call
  into that mechanism: this page deliberately doesn't set isV6Home for
  /playground/hub. Overriding the `header` block (rather than adding this
  markup inside {% block content %}) is what keeps it full-bleed — `header`
  renders outside the page's .govuk-width-container (see govuk-frontend's
  own template.njk), so the same markup placed in `content` instead ends up
  nested inside that container (plus its own inner one), visibly
  constraining the green background rather than spanning edge to edge.
  super() keeps the real top bar (logo, service name, sign-out link) from
  common/layouts/base.njk unchanged; this just appends the hero after it.
#}
{% block header %}
  {{ super() }}
  <div class="defra-home-header">
    <div class="govuk-width-container">
      <h1 class="defra-home-header__title">RPA Guidance hub</h1>
      <p class="defra-home-header__description">Find guidance to help you review and process claims, or manage guidance documents if you're responsible for keeping them up to date.</p>
      {% if navigation and navigation.length %}
        <nav class="defra-home-header__tabs" aria-label="Service navigation">
          <ul class="defra-home-header__tabs-list">
            {% for item in navigation %}
              <li class="defra-home-header__tabs-item">
                <a class="defra-home-header__tab{% if item.current %} defra-home-header__tab--active{% endif %}" href="{{ item.href }}"{% if item.current %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ item.text }}</a>
              </li>
            {% endfor %}
          </ul>
        </nav>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
{% endblock %}

{#
  Just the number — the "Version" column header next to it already says
  what it is. Identical in both retired templates; one copy is enough now
  they're merged.
#}
{% set versionTags = {
  "Version 1": { text: "1", classes: "govuk-tag--green" },
  "Version 2": { text: "2", classes: "govuk-tag--purple" }
} %}

{#
  Green/grey/yellow, same labels/colours as document-overview.html's own
  statusTags (app/views/versions/v6/manage-guidance/document-overview.html)
  — one badge per tab here, not per document: every row within a given
  tab shares the same state (every Recently opened/Saved guidance row is
  a real guidance-documents.js entry, which has no draft/review concept of
  its own — those are all Published; every Editing row is Draft; every
  Awaiting approval row is Awaiting approval), so the four macro call
  sites below each pass one fixed status string rather than reading a
  per-row field that doesn't exist.
#}
{% set statusTags = {
  "Published": { text: "Published", classes: "govuk-tag--green" },
  "Draft": { text: "Draft", classes: "govuk-tag--grey" },
  "Awaiting approval": { text: "Awaiting approval", classes: "govuk-tag--yellow" }
} %}

{#
  From find-guidance.html, with a status badge (statusCell, always
  "Published" — see statusTags' own comment above) added above the title
  link — both the Recently opened and Saved guidance panels below call
  this with their own row list and Remove-link ?tab= value.
#}
{% macro documentsTable(documents, removeWord, tabName, status) %}
  {% set rows = [] %}
  {% set statusCell %}<div class="govuk-!-margin-bottom-1">{{ govukTag(statusTags[status]) }}</div>{% endset %}
  {% for doc in documents %}
    {% set titleCell %}{{ statusCell | safe }}<a class="govuk-link" href="/playground/document/{{ doc.id }}">{{ doc.title }}</a>{% endset %}
    {% set versionCell %}{{ govukTag(versionTags[doc.version]) }}{% endset %}
    {% set actionCell %}
      <a class="govuk-link" href="/playground/hub/remove-confirm?id={{ doc.id }}&amp;tab={{ tabName }}">
        {{ removeWord }}<span class="govuk-visually-hidden"> {{ doc.title }}</span>
      </a>
    {% endset %}
    {% set rows = (rows.push([
      { html: titleCell },
      { text: doc.lastModified },
      { html: versionCell },
      { html: actionCell }
    ]), rows) %}
  {% endfor %}

  {{ govukTable({
    head: [
      { text: "Title", classes: "govuk-!-width-one-half" },
      { text: "Last modified" },
      { text: "Version" },
      { text: "Action" }
    ],
    rows: rows
  }) }}
{% endmacro %}

{#
  From all-guidance-docs.html, with a status badge (statusCell, "Draft" for
  the Editing tab — see statusTags' own comment above) added above the
  document name link, otherwise unchanged, including its own column split:
  columns == "checks" (Awaiting approval) shows Publishing checks/Changes
  requested with no Action column; the other branch (Editing, called with
  "lastModified") shows Last modified plus a Remove link instead. The two
  tabs diverged enough on the old page that one shared column set never
  fit both — that is still true here, so this keeps taking which columns
  to render as its own argument rather than assuming.

  No badge on the Awaiting approval tab specifically (columns == "checks")
  — every row there is already, by definition, awaiting approval, so a
  repeated "Awaiting approval" tag above each title added nothing the tab
  itself doesn't already say. The Editing tab keeps its "Draft" badge:
  unlike Awaiting approval, a document only lands there because it is
  Draft, but "Draft" is still a real status distinction worth restating
  next to a title (a document can leave Editing by either publishing or
  moving to Awaiting approval, so the badge is not pure repetition the way
  it was here).
#}
{% macro manageGuidanceTable(documents, columns, status) %}
  {% set rows = [] %}
  {% set statusCell %}<div class="govuk-!-margin-bottom-1">{{ govukTag(statusTags[status]) }}</div>{% endset %}
  {% for document in documents %}
    {% set nameCell %}{{ (statusCell | safe) if columns != "checks" }}<a class="govuk-link" href="/playground/document/{{ document.id }}">{{ document.name }}</a>{% endset %}
    {% set versionCell %}{{ govukTag(versionTags[document.version]) }}{% endset %}
    {% if columns == "checks" %}
      {% set checksText %}{% if document.publishingChecks == 0 %}No issues{% else %}{{ document.publishingChecks }} issue{{ "s" if document.publishingChecks != 1 }}{% endif %}{% endset %}
      {% set changesText %}{% if document.changesRequested == 0 %}None{% else %}{{ document.changesRequested }} change{{ "s" if document.changesRequested != 1 }} requested{% endif %}{% endset %}
      {% set rows = (rows.push([
        { html: nameCell },
        { html: versionCell },
        { text: checksText },
        { text: changesText }
      ]), rows) %}
    {% else %}
      {% set actionCell %}
        <a class="govuk-link" href="/playground/hub/remove-confirm?id={{ document.id }}&amp;tab=editing">
          Remove<span class="govuk-visually-hidden"> {{ document.name }}</span>
        </a>
      {% endset %}
      {% set rows = (rows.push([
        { html: nameCell },
        { html: versionCell },
        { text: document.lastModified },
        { html: actionCell }
      ]), rows) %}
    {% endif %}
  {% endfor %}

  {% if columns == "checks" %}
    {{ govukTable({
      head: [
        { text: "Document name", classes: "govuk-!-width-one-half" },
        { text: "Version" },
        { text: "Publishing checks" },
        { text: "Changes requested" }
      ],
      rows: rows
    }) }}
  {% else %}
    {{ govukTable({
      head: [
        { text: "Document name", classes: "govuk-!-width-one-half" },
        { text: "Version" },
        { text: "Last modified" },
        { html: '<span class="govuk-visually-hidden">Action</span>' }
      ],
      rows: rows
    }) }}
  {% endif %}
{% endmacro %}

{#
  A plain "Search guidance" <h2 class="govuk-heading-m"> plus a one-line
  govuk-hint underneath it ("Search using guidance title or description")
  — a later pass re-added a subtext line here, styled as GDS hint text
  (secondary/muted, smaller than govuk-body) rather than the fuller
  explanatory paragraph an earlier pass removed entirely (see the design
  refinement note at the top of this file for that history) — a short
  hint, not a repeat of that longer copy. govuk-heading-m, not -l, for the
  same reason the per-tab panel headings further down use -m: a real GDS
  heading step, but one step below the page's actual <h1> in the green
  banner rather than matching its size.

  One search bar now, not two — routed unconditionally to
  /v6/manage-guidance/search-guidance (the filterable Category/State/
  Scheme/Year results page) regardless of which tab is active, per an
  explicit request that the hub's own search always go there rather than
  switching between that and /v6/find-guidance/organic-search depending on
  the tab group. The previous findGuidanceSearch/manageGuidanceSearch
  split (one search bar per tab *group*, each pointing at its own
  destination, toggled by data-search-group and a TAB_SEARCH_GROUP map in
  pageScripts) is gone entirely along with the second destination — always
  visible now, not toggled with the active tab at all.
#}
{% set searchGuidance %}
  <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Search guidance</h2>
  <p class="govuk-hint">Search using guidance title or description</p>
  <form method="get" action="/playground/hub/search">
    <div class="app-search-bar">
      <div class="app-search-bar__input">
        {{ govukInput({
          id: "unified-guidance-search",
          name: "q",
          label: { text: "Search guidance", classes: "govuk-visually-hidden" },
          formGroup: { classes: "govuk-!-margin-bottom-0" }
        }) }}
      </div>
      {{ govukButton({
        text: "Search",
        classes: "govuk-!-margin-bottom-0"
      }) }}
    </div>
  </form>
{% endset %}

{% block content %}

<div class="govuk-grid-row">
  <div class="govuk-grid-column-full">

    <div class="app-unified-guidance__search">
      {{ searchGuidance | safe }}
    </div>

    {{ govukButton({ text: "Upload guide", href: "/playground/upload" }) }}

  </div>
</div>

<div class="govuk-grid-row">
  <div class="govuk-grid-column-full">

    {#
      Real govuk-tabs markup (see the top-of-file comment for why this is
      hand-written rather than the govukTabs() macro/its data-module JS).
      href="#tab-panel-x" is kept — matching genuine govuk-tabs output —
      purely so each tab still resolves to a real, in-page id if JS is
      somehow unavailable; pageScripts' click handler calls
      preventDefault() on every click, so in the normal case it never
      actually navigates via the anchor or touches location.hash (?tab= is
      this page's own deep-linking scheme instead — see view-model.js).
    #}
    <div class="govuk-tabs">

      <ul class="govuk-tabs__list" role="tablist" aria-label="Guidance sections">
        <li class="govuk-tabs__list-item{% if activeTab == "recently-opened" %} govuk-tabs__list-item--selected{% endif %}" role="presentation">
          <a class="govuk-tabs__tab" href="#tab-panel-recently-opened"
             data-tab-button="recently-opened" id="tab-button-recently-opened"
             role="tab" aria-selected="{{ "true" if activeTab == "recently-opened" else "false" }}"
             aria-controls="tab-panel-recently-opened">
            Recently opened ({{ recentlyOpenedDocuments.length }})
          </a>
        </li>
        <li class="govuk-tabs__list-item{% if activeTab == "saved-guidance" %} govuk-tabs__list-item--selected{% endif %}" role="presentation">
          <a class="govuk-tabs__tab" href="#tab-panel-saved-guidance"
             data-tab-button="saved-guidance" id="tab-button-saved-guidance"
             role="tab" aria-selected="{{ "true" if activeTab == "saved-guidance" else "false" }}"
             aria-controls="tab-panel-saved-guidance">
            Saved guidance ({{ savedGuidanceDocuments.length }})
          </a>
        </li>
        <li class="govuk-tabs__list-item{% if activeTab == "editing" %} govuk-tabs__list-item--selected{% endif %}" role="presentation">
          <a class="govuk-tabs__tab" href="#tab-panel-editing"
             data-tab-button="editing" id="tab-button-editing"
             role="tab" aria-selected="{{ "true" if activeTab == "editing" else "false" }}"
             aria-controls="tab-panel-editing">
            Editing ({{ editingDocuments.length }})
          </a>
        </li>
        <li class="govuk-tabs__list-item{% if activeTab == "awaiting-approval" %} govuk-tabs__list-item--selected{% endif %}" role="presentation">
          <a class="govuk-tabs__tab" href="#tab-panel-awaiting-approval"
             data-tab-button="awaiting-approval" id="tab-button-awaiting-approval"
             role="tab" aria-selected="{{ "true" if activeTab == "awaiting-approval" else "false" }}"
             aria-controls="tab-panel-awaiting-approval">
            Awaiting approval ({{ awaitingApprovalDocuments.length }})
          </a>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <div class="govuk-tabs__panel{% if activeTab != "recently-opened" %} govuk-tabs__panel--hidden{% endif %}"
           data-tab-panel="recently-opened" id="tab-panel-recently-opened"
           role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-button-recently-opened">
        <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Recently opened</h2>
        <p class="govuk-hint">Your {{ recentlyOpenedDocuments.length }} recently opened guidances</p>
        {{ documentsTable(recentlyOpenedDocuments, "Remove", "recently-opened", "Published") }}
      </div>

      <div class="govuk-tabs__panel{% if activeTab != "saved-guidance" %} govuk-tabs__panel--hidden{% endif %}"
           data-tab-panel="saved-guidance" id="tab-panel-saved-guidance"
           role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-button-saved-guidance">
        <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Saved guidance</h2>
        <p class="govuk-hint">Guidance you've saved for quick access.</p>
        {{ documentsTable(savedGuidanceDocuments, "Remove", "saved-guidance", "Published") }}
      </div>

      <div class="govuk-tabs__panel{% if activeTab != "editing" %} govuk-tabs__panel--hidden{% endif %}"
           data-tab-panel="editing" id="tab-panel-editing"
           role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-button-editing">
        <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Editing</h2>
        <p class="govuk-hint">All your guidance in edit mode appears here. Make changes and save progress as you work.</p>
        {{ manageGuidanceTable(editingDocuments, "lastModified", "Draft") }}
      </div>

      <div class="govuk-tabs__panel{% if activeTab != "awaiting-approval" %} govuk-tabs__panel--hidden{% endif %}"
           data-tab-panel="awaiting-approval" id="tab-panel-awaiting-approval"
           role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-button-awaiting-approval">
        <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Awaiting approval</h2>
        <p class="govuk-hint">Guidance pending review and approval before publishing. Publishing checks verify that your guidance meets quality standards before publishing.</p>
        {{ manageGuidanceTable(awaitingApprovalDocuments, "checks", "Awaiting approval") }}
      </div>

    </div>

  </div>
</div>

{% endblock %}

{% block pageScripts %}
  <script>
    (function () {
      // Generic data-tab-button/data-tab-panel switch — same mechanism
      // app/views/versions/v6/editor-2-3-view.html's own Content/Comments/
      // Checks tabs already use, copied rather than shared from a common
      // file (matching how every other instance of this pattern in this
      // project is its own inline copy, not a shared script), driving the
      // exact same classes real govuk-tabs.js would (--selected/--hidden)
      // without using that script itself — see the top-of-file comment
      // for why. activeTab (view-model.js) has already set the correct
      // tab/panel active server-side, so this only needs to handle clicks
      // from there — no need to re-read ?tab= on load.
      var tabButtons = document.querySelectorAll('[data-tab-button]')

      tabButtons.forEach(function (tabButton) {
        tabButton.addEventListener('click', function (event) {
          // Each tab is a real <a href="#tab-panel-x"> (matching genuine
          // govuk-tabs markup) — without this, a click would jump-scroll
          // to the panel and set location.hash, competing with this
          // page's own ?tab= deep-linking below.
          event.preventDefault()

          tabButtons.forEach(function (button) {
            var active = button === tabButton
            button.closest('.govuk-tabs__list-item').classList.toggle('govuk-tabs__list-item--selected', active)
            button.setAttribute('aria-selected', String(active))

            var panel = document.querySelector('[data-tab-panel="' + button.dataset.tabButton + '"]')
            if (panel) panel.classList.toggle('govuk-tabs__panel--hidden', !active)
          })

          // Keeps the address bar (so it can be copied/bookmarked/refreshed
          // back to the same tab) in sync without adding a browser-history
          // entry per click — replaceState, not pushState, so Back leaves
          // the page instead of stepping backward through tabs.
          var url = new URL(window.location)
          url.searchParams.set('tab', tabButton.dataset.tabButton)
          window.history.replaceState(null, '', url)
        })
      })
    })()
  </script>
{% endblock %}
